
========================================================================
FIXTURES — built, not asserted
========================================================================
built: foreign badsource slashes ours plain

========================================================================
PROOF 1 — a FOREIGN but well-formed source must fail the OWNERSHIP check.
This is the case that is GREEN today and must not be. `oven-sh/bun` is two
clean lowercase segments with exactly one slash: it passes every grammar in the
file, so shape cannot see it. Only --expect-source can.
========================================================================

--- expect 5 (mismatch)
$ sh docker/provenance.sh --verify kit-owns-proof:foreign --expect-source cafaye/guard
provenance: kit-owns-proof:foreign
  source:           oven-sh/bun
  revision:         0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
  built_at:         2026-10-03T09:20:00Z
  source_dirty:     clean
  template_version: v0.1.0
kit-provenance: FAIL kit-owns-proof:foreign is built from oven-sh/bun, and cafaye/guard was expected.
kit-provenance:   a stamp that satisfies the grammar is not a stamp that is OURS. oven-sh/bun is a
kit-provenance:   well-formed and entirely foreign, which is the case shape cannot see.
EXIT=5

--- expect 5 (and no revision expectation: the flag form)
$ sh docker/provenance.sh --verify kit-owns-proof:foreign --expect-source cafaye/guard --expect-revision 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
provenance: kit-owns-proof:foreign
  source:           oven-sh/bun
  revision:         0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
  built_at:         2026-10-03T09:20:00Z
  source_dirty:     clean
  template_version: v0.1.0
kit-provenance: FAIL kit-owns-proof:foreign is built from oven-sh/bun, and cafaye/guard was expected.
kit-provenance:   a stamp that satisfies the grammar is not a stamp that is OURS. oven-sh/bun is a
kit-provenance:   well-formed and entirely foreign, which is the case shape cannot see.
EXIT=5

========================================================================
PROOF 2 — a label violating the SHAPE grammar must fail on shape, with the
expect_* line, even though the ownership check would also have failed. The URL
is over the one-slash budget; `cafaye/guard/labels` is over it the other way.
========================================================================

--- expect 6 (URL source)
$ sh docker/provenance.sh --verify kit-owns-proof:badsource --expect-source cafaye/guard
provenance: kit-owns-proof:badsource
  source:           https://github.com/cafaye/guard
  revision:         0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
  built_at:         2026-10-03T09:20:00Z
  source_dirty:     clean
  template_version: v0.1.0
kit-provenance: FAIL kit-owns-proof:badsource carries labels, and they are not a cafaye provenance stamp.
kit-provenance:   source           = "https://github.com/cafaye/guard" — it must be owner/repo, or "unknown" (lowercase, exactly one "/", no scheme, no host, no port)
kit-provenance:   org.opencontainers.image.* are STANDARD OCI labels that every base image sets,
kit-provenance:   and an image built FROM a stamped one INHERITS them. This stamp names "https://github.com/cafaye/guard",
kit-provenance:   which is not us. A verifier a third party's labels can satisfy is not a verifier.
EXIT=6

--- expect 6 (three segments)
$ sh docker/provenance.sh --verify kit-owns-proof:slashes --expect-source cafaye/guard
provenance: kit-owns-proof:slashes
  source:           cafaye/guard/labels
  revision:         0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
  built_at:         2026-10-03T09:20:00Z
  source_dirty:     clean
  template_version: v0.1.0
kit-provenance: FAIL kit-owns-proof:slashes carries labels, and they are not a cafaye provenance stamp.
kit-provenance:   source           = "cafaye/guard/labels" — it must be owner/repo, or "unknown" (lowercase, exactly one "/", no scheme, no host, no port)
kit-provenance:   org.opencontainers.image.* are STANDARD OCI labels that every base image sets,
kit-provenance:   and an image built FROM a stamped one INHERITS them. This stamp names "cafaye/guard/labels",
kit-provenance:   which is not us. A verifier a third party's labels can satisfy is not a verifier.
EXIT=6

========================================================================
PROOF 3 — a correct stamp with a MATCHING --expect-source must exit 0.
========================================================================

--- expect 0
$ sh docker/provenance.sh --verify kit-owns-proof:ours --expect-source cafaye/guard --expect-revision 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
provenance: kit-owns-proof:ours
  source:           cafaye/guard
  revision:         0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
  built_at:         2026-10-03T09:20:00Z
  source_dirty:     clean
  template_version: v0.1.0
kit-provenance: ok kit-owns-proof:ours is 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
EXIT=0

========================================================================
PROOF 3b — the SAME image with NO --expect-source: exit 0 plus the loud
ownership warning. The overrule, measured: a warning, not a failure.
========================================================================

--- expect 0 + WARN
$ sh docker/provenance.sh --verify kit-owns-proof:ours
provenance: kit-owns-proof:ours
  source:           cafaye/guard
  revision:         0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
  built_at:         2026-10-03T09:20:00Z
  source_dirty:     clean
  template_version: v0.1.0
kit-provenance: WARN no --expect-source was given, so OWNERSHIP OF THE REPOSITORY WAS NOT ESTABLISHED.
kit-provenance:      the source reads "cafaye/guard", and every grammar in this file accepts it. Only
kit-provenance:      --expect-source owner/repo turns "it is shaped like ours" into "it IS ours".
EXIT=0

